Cell grid:
  efforts: e5, e7, e9
  distances: 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0
  strategies: Zenjxl (default, all wins on) + Libjxl (strict cjxl-parity gate)
  reference: cjxl 0.12.0 -e {effort} -d {distance} --quiet

Total: 20 images × 3 efforts × 4 distances = 240 cells × 3 encodes = 720 encodes.
Wall: 534.5s (8.9 min initial pass) + 31.4s (gui re-run after alpha fix)
      = 566s ≈ 9.4 min total. Well under the ~60 min budget.

Bench-tooling bugs found + fixed mid-flight:
  1. score_jxl() truncated jxl-oxide RGBA output via `chunks_exact(3)`,
     producing SSIM2 ≈ -204 on gui.png (the only RGBA image). FIX: detect
     channel count via dec_lin.len() / (dw*dh) and slice accordingly. Cells
     for gui.png re-run with `--only gui` after fix.
  2. No other corpus images had alpha (verified via `identify -format
     "%[channels]"`). codec_wiki + 3 photos + 5 CLIC all sRGB.

